BT 1 0 0 1 0 58 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL 1.074651 Tw (Caching means keeping a copy of frequently accessed data somewhere closer and faster than its original) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.112512 Tw (source, usually in memory, so that repeated requests for the same data do not have to pay the full cost again.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.419431 Tw (The database remains the source of truth. The cache is just a fast, temporary shortcut to data you have) Tj T* 0 Tw (already fetched once.) Tj T* ET
