BT 1 0 0 1 0 58 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL -0.087791 Tw (Redis is an in-memory key-value store. Data is held in RAM, which is what makes reads and writes extremely) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.074016 Tw (fast compared to a disk-backed database. It also supports persistence to disk, through snapshotting \(RDB\) or) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.11186 Tw (an append-only log \(AOF\), so a restart does not always mean losing everything, though most teams treat) Tj T* 0 Tw (cached data as something that can be safely rebuilt if it is lost.) Tj T* ET
