BT 1 0 0 1 0 75 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL 1.028988 Tw (Notice what this means for the first request after the cache is empty, or after a key has expired. That first) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.287356 Tw (request is always slower, because it has to pay the full database cost plus the cost of writing into Redis.) Tj T* 0 Tw .058409 Tw (Every request after that, until the key expires again, is fast. This is exactly the tradeoff you are accepting with) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.63311 Tw (cache-aside, and it is worth saying out loud in an interview rather than pretending caching makes every) Tj T* 0 Tw (single request fast.) Tj T* ET
