BT 1 0 0 1 0 63 Tm /F1 9.5 Tf 14.5 TL (Cache-aside keeps your database as the single source of truth and only fails soft, a cache miss just means) Tj T* (a slower request, not a wrong one. The cost is that the first reader after an eviction always pays full price,) Tj T* (and a busy key that keeps expiring can repeatedly hammer the database. Write-through avoids stale reads) Tj T* (but slows down every write. There is no universally correct choice here, the right one depends on whether) Tj T* (your workload is read-heavy or write-heavy.) Tj T* ET
