BT 1 0 0 1 12 182 Tm (When asked 'why Kafka over RabbitMQ?', cover three points:) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 165 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 148 Tm (1. Kafka retains messages on disk for a configurable time. RabbitMQ deletes) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 134 Tm (once consumed.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 117 Tm (2. Kafka supports multiple independent consumer groups reading the same) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 103 Tm (topic. RabbitMQ delivers each message to one consumer.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 86 Tm (3. Kafka scales via partitions and handles millions of events per second.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 72 Tm (RabbitMQ is simpler but doesn't match that throughput.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 55 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 38 Tm (Then add: 'For a simple task queue with retries, RabbitMQ is valid. Kafka) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 12 24 Tm (makes more sense when I need event replay or fan-out at scale.') Tj T* ET
