BT 1 0 0 1 0 75 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL 1.475251 Tw (Here is a scenario I have seen play out in real projects more than once. A Spring Boot service starts) Tj T* 0 Tw .235542 Tw (slowing down under load. Someone on the team says "just bump up the EC2 instance size," and it works.) Tj T* 0 Tw .388651 Tw (CPU usage drops, response times improve, everyone moves on. Three months later, the same service is) Tj T* 0 Tw .630542 Tw (struggling again, except now there is no bigger instance left to move to. That is vertical scaling hitting its) Tj T* 0 Tw (ceiling, and it always hits one.) Tj T* ET
