BT 1 0 0 1 0 75 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL .969269 Tw (Horizontal scaling means adding more machines instead of making one machine bigger. Instead of one) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.091265 Tw (Spring Boot instance handling everything, you run five or ten instances, and a load balancer spreads traffic) Tj T* 0 Tw .243516 Tw (across them. This is where things get interesting for an interview, because horizontal scaling is not free. It) Tj T* 0 Tw .784431 Tw (demands that your service behaves a certain way, and that is exactly what the next topic in this module) Tj T* 0 Tw (covers.) Tj T* ET
