BT 1 0 0 1 0 75 Tm /F1 10 Tf 17 TL .495984 Tw (In production, things break all the time. Not because engineers are bad, but because distributed systems) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.643828 Tw (are inherently unreliable. Networks drop packets. Databases get slow under load. Third-party APIs go) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.341654 Tw (down. A memory leak in one service can make it unresponsive for minutes. Your job is not to prevent) Tj T* 0 Tw .105542 Tw (every failure. It is to build systems that handle failures gracefully and keep working even when parts of the) Tj T* 0 Tw (system are broken.) Tj T* ET
