BT 1 0 0 1 0 75 Tm .587209 Tw 17 TL /F1 10 Tf .901961 .929412 .952941 rg (Plaintext passwords in a database is the obvious sin nobody admits to in an interview, but a more common) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.259461 Tw (real mistake is using a fast hash like MD5 or SHA-256 directly on the password. Fast hashes exist to be) Tj T* 0 Tw .409984 Tw (quick, which is exactly the wrong property for password storage, since it makes brute-forcing leaked hashes) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.633318 Tw (cheap. The correct tools are slow-by-design: bcrypt, scrypt, or Argon2. In Spring Security, this is just) Tj T* 0 Tw /F4 10 Tf .247059 .72549 .313725 rg (BCryptPasswordEncoder) Tj /F1 10 Tf .901961 .929412 .952941 rg (, and there's rarely a good reason to swap it for something else.) Tj T* ET
