BT 1 0 0 1 0 63 Tm /F1 9.5 Tf 14.5 TL .262382 Tw (If an interviewer asks why the client does not just send the file straight to S3 without asking your backend) Tj T* 0 Tw .449163 Tw (first, the answer is access control. The backend decides who is allowed to upload, validates file type and) Tj T* 0 Tw .262516 Tw (size before a single byte moves, and generates the storage key itself so users cannot pick arbitrary paths) Tj T* 0 Tw .747209 Tw (in your bucket. The presigned URL is also short-lived, ten minutes is typical, so it cannot be leaked and) Tj T* 0 Tw (reused later. It is permission to do one specific upload, not an open door.) Tj T* ET
