BT 1 0 0 1 14 89 Tm (For an Instagram-style feed, the core design decisions are: use the Transactional Outbox pattern so post) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 76 Tm (events reach Kafka reliably, fan-out on write for normal users and fan-out on read for celebrities, cache the first) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 63 Tm (feed page in Redis, store feed_items in Cassandra partitioned by user_id, and always serve media from CDN.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 50 Tm (The tradeoff is write-time cost versus read-time latency, and the hybrid strategy is what real systems use.) Tj T* ET
