BT 1 0 0 1 14 102 Tm (For a YouTube-style video upload system, the core decisions are: use presigned URLs so video bytes go) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 89 Tm (directly to object storage and never touch your API servers, use async transcoding workers so upload is fast) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 76 Tm (and processing happens in the background, use the Transactional Outbox Pattern so Kafka events are) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 63 Tm (published only after the DB commits, and use CDN so viewers stream from the edge, not from your backend.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 50 Tm (The tradeoff is complexity of coordination versus bandwidth and scalability at each step.) Tj T* ET
