BT 1 0 0 1 14 336 Tm (1. Open with scope. "We are designing centralized logging for microservices: collection, search, and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 323 Tm (retention. Not full observability with metrics and tracing." 30 seconds.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 305 Tm (2. State the key constraint immediately. "Logging must never block the request path. Apps write locally,) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 292 Tm (shipping happens async." This sentence shows real production experience. 30 seconds.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 274 Tm (3. Draw the architecture. App ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( stdout ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Collector ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Kafka ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Processor ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Hot Store + Cold Archive ) Tj /F5 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\256) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 261 Tm (Dashboard/Alerting. 2 minutes.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 243 Tm (4. Explain the hot/cold split. Recent logs in a search engine for fast debugging. Old logs compressed in object) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 230 Tm (storage for cheap retention. One sentence each. 1 minute.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 212 Tm (5. Walk through the flow. Request comes in, MDC gets traceId, structured JSON log written to stdout, collector) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 199 Tm (ships to Kafka, processor masks PII and indexes. 2 minutes.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 181 Tm (6. Cover one failure. Kafka goes down: collector buffers locally with a size cap, drops lowest priority first.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 168 Tm (This shows you think about backpressure. 1.5 minutes.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 150 Tm (7. Close with one tradeoff. Structured JSON vs plain text, or hot/cold storage split. Pick one and explain it with) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 14 137 Tm (confidence. 1.5 minutes.) Tj T* ET
